The topology generated by the pointwise subbasis on Scott maps equals the topology induced from the product of copies of the Scott topology on the codomain.

Continuity into the induced topology reduces to continuity of each evaluation, and the preimage of a Scott-open set under evaluation is a pointwise subbasic set. In the other direction, each pointwise subbasic set is the preimage of a subbasic open of that product, because evaluation is continuous for the product of Scott topologies.
